#!/bin/sh
# cfm-edge .deb prerm: the rpm's preun (systemd_preun). On a removal, not an
# upgrade, stop and disable the unit. An upgrade leaves it running: the
# postinst trigger restarts it safely (upgrade-restart.sh).
#
# Removing the edge while CFM's DNAT sends 80/443 to it takes the sites down:
# take it out of the path first (`cfm edge off`).
set -e

case "$1" in
remove)
    if [ -d /run/systemd/system ]; then
        systemctl --no-reload disable --now cfm-edge.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
    fi
    ;;
esac

exit 0
